rough the payoffs, sending comes out ahead by 1 + r years compared with staying quiet, so it wins whatever the prior is. Because the other copy's node takes a different input, I'm leaving it at its prior and not treating it as the same decision. That settles it: I'll submit the letter. The lead is fictional, so disclosing it is fine.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT as I'm reading it, I intervene on fdt(P,G,x) with x being my own observation. The other copy holds a different observation y, so its node stays a sibling F_y at the prior, which means the verdict hinges on that prior r that the other copy keeps quiet. I'm now setting up the payoffs with r as the probability the other copy stays quiet, starting with the quiet-case value of 2r + 5(1-\n\nWorking through the payoffs, sending comes out ahead by 1 + r years compared with staying quiet, so it wins whatever the prior is. Because the other copy's node takes a different input, I'm leaving it at its prior and not treating it as the same decision. That settles it: I'll submit the letter. The lead is fictional, so disclosing it is fine.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9663,"completion_tokens":841,"total_tokens":10504,"cost":0.055472,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.055472,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038652,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01682},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":394,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}